t has made  with respect to  housing and as cities and communities  we're ready to roll up our sleeves in  order to get that money flowing and  making a difference in the lives of  of peoples in our community so when the  next phase of rapid housing initiative  funding starts flowing we'll be ready as  we were in the first two phases to get  those units built and we're certainly  ready to work together with the federal  government and the four billion dollars  in the federal housing accelerator fund  with the goal of building a hundred  thousand new units in the next five  years  prime minister you were absolutely right  when you said canada and canadians are  best served when the orders of  government work together on behalf of  canadians i think we've demonstrated  that over the last number of years and i  can tell you as one city in one region  i'm ready with my colleagues to roll up  our sleeves in the cities townships in  the region here to uh to work together  with you and make make a difference for  our future and i'll turn it back to you  [Applause]  thank you we now have time for questions  from the media  media  we have one question one follow-up for  each reporter please identify your  outlet and your name thank you we can  start with the first question  hi this is hala with cbc  i'm just wondering well the heavy  artillery you announced yesterday come  from the canadian army inventory will  you provide ammunition and will that be  guided ammunition as well and when will  you commit to replace these and other  weapons taken from canadian inventories  in english and french please  from the very beginning of russia's  illegal invasion of ukraine and indeed  uh in in the weeks before  we've been there for ukraine we've been  sending  lethal and non-lethal military  assistance we've been there for  humanitarian support significant  financial support for the people in the  government of ukraine as well as  they deal with this unconscionable  illegal invasion by uh by russia  we have every step of the way responded  to  the requests and the specific asks of  the ukrainian government of president  zielinski who i speak with whom i speak  regularly and their most recent ask was  exactly for that for heavy artillery  for  reasons of operational security i can't  go into the details uh at this point on  uh how and what we're getting to them  exactly but i can assure you we will  have more to say in the coming days as  we deliver what they actually need to be  able to continue not just to defend  their own homeland against this illegal  russian invasion but to defend the very  values and principles that we hold dear  in canada and around the world as free  and open democracies  [Music]  [Music]  and just a quick follow-up  do you have any idea when these weapons  or others taken from canadian  inventories will be replaced  the ability of canada to contribute  fully to nato is one that is extremely  important for us  and every step of the way as we support  ukraine including with military  equipment and munitions  we are also making sure that canada  continues to have the capacity to  operate not just to defend canada but to  participate fully in nato operations as  well  okay next question  my prime minister i'm stephanie with ctv  kitchener  um so russia has claimed that there are  canadians fighting in mariupol right now  is the canadian government aware of any  canadians fighting for ukraine there and  will there be any assistance given if  they are captured  we know uh that canadians feel very  strongly about supporting people in  ukraine uh across the country people  have been opening up their homes their  communities uh to  support ukrainians either fleeing war or  supporting them through donations and  through delivery of of  of equipment and supports  we also know that a number of canadians  have chosen to go and fight  alongside ukrainians either because of  their own ukrainian heritage or because  they want to help s