ars and  anyone who's promising that they have a  quick fix for it  is not being straight with canadians  it's going to take all of us working  together to curb foreign speculation to  make sure that market is fairer to  create more housing units and offer and  to support families being able to save  up to do that and that's very much what  we're focused on thank you prime  minister one follow-up question  different topic we do not currently have  a member of parliament a member of  parliament in this region in cabinet  with the departure of bartis jagger from  cabinet recently is uh  why is that and will your government  rectify that important area and we've  had cabinet membership for many years we  continue to have an amazing team of  strong mps and ministers from across the  country who are focused on this region  on the growing  challenges and opportunities in southern  ontario and i can assure you  that all of us do a great job making  sure we're speaking to and for all  canadians but as always we're looking at  to grow the teams in coming elections  and we're going to continue to stay  connected with canadians and build the  kind of team that is responsive to what  canadians need next question  good morning prime minister liam casey  with the canadian press um major group  of uh major group helping veterans um  transition network to get interpreters  out of afghanistan they're winding down  operations  you know because they say there's  bureaucratic cubes that are blocking  efforts to get paperwork and causing  this bottleneck  what do you have to say to the  interpreters who risked their lives to  help canada and now feel  abandoned by your government the  situation in afghanistan is  heartbreaking  the  taking over that country by the taliban  has made it unbelievably difficult  not just for canadians who served and  sacrificed to build a better future for  afghans but also to people who want to  welcome people who've supported them  to canada we have  acce